cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use cma-mcp in academic, applied, or compliance work,
  please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "cma-mcp: MCP server for the cma command on PATH"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lucic
    given-names: Lovro
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9976-6933"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/cma-mcp/"
abstract: >-
  cma-mcp is an MCP server that runs the cma command on PATH. It
  stores nothing itself. The notes, the file match, and the counts
  are whatever that cma binary does. An older cma earlier on PATH
  is the one that runs. It does not measure whether a note changes
  the next failure.
keywords:
  - mcp
  - model-context-protocol
  - compound-practice
  - failure-capture
  - decision-tracking
  - prevention
  - cma
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.7"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: "https://pypi.org/project/cma-mcp/"
    description: "PyPI distribution"
references:
  - type: software
    title: "cma: notes you write, shown again on a later edit"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lucic
        given-names: Lovro
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9976-6933"
    license: Apache-2.0
    notes: "The canonical reference implementation that cma-mcp wraps. cma-mcp invokes its CLI as a subprocess; the data substrate (`~/.cma/*.jsonl`) is shared between cma and cma-mcp."
